{
  "title": "About Rcntimeline Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The RCN Timeline plugin puts a small timeline on a wiki page: each interval a bar, its uncertain edges fading in and out, the links between intervals drawn as curves, and a date axis across the top. Hover a bar for its dates, who says so, how sure they are, and any note. Click a bar and its page opens in the lineup beside this one.",
      "id": "f0a9a8322aafc9ab"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "029356e7e8442a58",
      "text": "See [https://github.com/marpie1/rcn/tree/master/wiki-plugin-rcntimeline GitHub] for plugin source."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The full RCN Timeline tool solves and edits: it moves floating intervals to satisfy their links and flags contradictions. This plugin only draws what the item holds, dates as stored.",
      "id": "b1685103986c7744"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Editing the item. Double-click to open the text editor. The first line of the text is the caption; the rest lists the intervals and links in words, so wiki search finds them. The intervals themselves live in the item\u2019s timeline field, in the tool\u2019s own export format. A new item from the Factory has no timeline field yet: type lines such as Pilot = Jan 2020 .. Jun 2021 and each becomes a bar.",
      "id": "84d2ec6a4ab43717"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Below: the Northwest Agriculture Business Center, from the Co-ops of Whatcom County pages. Its help to the meat co-op sits inside the co-op\u2019s organising years, and the food hub it ran became a farmer-owned co-op.",
      "id": "8bd7dff26d7d8c1e"
    },
